<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 28 January, from 814 to 1986.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">814 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charlemagne dies at Aachen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Frankish king, crowned emperor in 800, died after ruling much of western Europe. His empire was divided among his grandsons within thirty years, but its memory shaped the Holy Roman Empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1547 CE <span class="tih-ago">479 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII dies at Whitehall</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry VIII died aged 55 after a reign that broke with Rome, dissolved the monasteries and saw six marriages. His nine-year-old son succeeded him as Edward VI.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1613 CE <span class="tih-ago">413 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo observes Neptune without recognising it</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Galileo's notes record a 'star' near Jupiter that was in fact Neptune, and even note that it seemed to move. The planet was not identified until 1846.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1807 CE <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gas lamps light Pall Mall in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frederick Albert Winsor's demonstration lit part of Pall Mall with gas lamps, the first public street lighting by gas. Gas lighting spread rapidly through British cities over the next decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1871 CE <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paris capitulates and France signs an armistice with Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a four-month siege, the French government agreed an armistice with the new German Empire. The peace that followed cost France Alsace and much of Lorraine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1932 CE <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japanese forces attack Shanghai</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese marines clashed with China's 19th Route Army in Shanghai, and Japanese aircraft bombed the Zhabei district. The fighting lasted over a month before a ceasefire was brokered.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1986 CE <span class="tih-ago">40 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Space Shuttle Challenger breaks apart after launch</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Challenger broke apart 73 seconds after lift-off, killing its seven crew, including teacher Christa McAuliffe. A faulty seal in a booster rocket was to blame, and shuttle flights stopped for 32 months.</p></div></li></ol>
